<file path=".github/workflows/ci.yml">
name: CI — Build, Test, and Frontend Validation

on:
  pull_request:
    branches:
      - dev
      - staging
      - main
    paths:
      - '.github/workflows/ci.yml'
      - '.gitignore'
      - 'XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.API/**'
      - 'XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Application/**'
      - 'XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Domain/**'
      - 'XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Gateway/**'
      - 'XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Infrastructure/**'
      - 'XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.SharedKernel/**'
      - 'XYDataLabs.OpenPayAdapter/**'
      - 'frontend/**'
      - 'frontend/.gitignore'
      - 'scripts/validate-tracked-generated-artifacts.ps1'
      - 'tests/**'
      - 'Resources/Configuration/**'
      - 'Directory.Build.props'
      - 'Directory.Packages.props'
      - '*.sln'

permissions:
  contents: read
  pull-requests: write

env:
  DOTNET_VERSION: '8.x'
  NODE_VERSION: '20.x'

jobs:
  build-and-test:
    name: Build and Test
    runs-on: windows-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v6

      - name: Validate tracked generated artifacts
        shell: pwsh
        run: scripts/validate-tracked-generated-artifacts.ps1

      - name: Set up .NET
        uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v5
        with:
          dotnet-version: ${{ env.DOTNET_VERSION }}

      - name: Set up Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: ${{ env.NODE_VERSION }}
          cache: npm
          cache-dependency-path: frontend/package-lock.json

      - name: Install frontend dependencies
        working-directory: frontend
        run: npm ci

      - name: Validate frontend type safety
        working-directory: frontend
        run: npm run typecheck

      - name: Test frontend workspace
        working-directory: frontend
        run: npm run test:web

      - name: Build frontend workspace
        working-directory: frontend
        run: npm run build

      - name: Restore dependencies
        run: dotnet restore XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.sln

      - name: Build solution
        run: dotnet build XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.sln --configuration Release --no-restore

      - name: Test — Domain
        run: dotnet test tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Domain.Tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Domain.Tests.csproj --configuration Release --no-build --verbosity normal

      - name: Test — Application
        run: dotnet test tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Application.Tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Application.Tests.csproj --configuration Release --no-build --verbosity normal

      - name: Test — API
        run: dotnet test tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.API.Tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.API.Tests.csproj --configuration Release --no-build --verbosity normal

      - name: Test — Gateway
        run: dotnet test tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Gateway.Tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Gateway.Tests.csproj --configuration Release --no-build --verbosity normal

      - name: Test — Architecture
        run: dotnet test tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Architecture.Tests/XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Architecture.Tests.csproj --configuration Release --no-build --verbosity normal

        # Integration tests require Testcontainers + Docker daemon (Linux containers).
        # windows-latest runner does not support Linux containers.
        # Run locally or promote to a dedicated linux runner when Testcontainers CI is needed.
</file>

<file path=".github/workflows/deploy-ui-to-azure.yml">
name: Deploy React Frontend to Azure App Service

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main
      - staging
      - dev
    paths:
      - 'frontend/**'
      - 'Resources/Configuration/**'
      - '.github/workflows/deploy-ui-to-azure.yml'
  workflow_dispatch:

env:
  NODE_VERSION: '20'
  AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME: ''
  FRONTEND_ARTIFACT_PATH: './react-web'

# This workflow builds and deploys the Track U React frontend to the existing UI App Service.

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: windows-latest
    permissions:
      contents: read
    outputs:
      apiBaseUrl: ${{ steps.resolve-target.outputs.apiBaseUrl }}

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v6

      - name: Set up Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v6
        with:
          node-version: ${{ env.NODE_VERSION }}
          cache: npm
          cache-dependency-path: frontend/package-lock.json

      - name: Validate frontend workspace sources
        shell: pwsh
        run: scripts/validate-tracked-generated-artifacts.ps1

      - name: Resolve target API base URL
        id: resolve-target
        shell: pwsh
        run: |
          $ref = "${{ github.ref }}"
          $owner = "${{ github.repository_owner }}".ToLowerInvariant()

          if ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/main') { $envSuffix = 'prod' }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/staging') { $envSuffix = 'stg' }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/dev') { $envSuffix = 'dev' }
          else { $branch = $ref.Replace('refs/heads/',''); $envSuffix = $branch }

          $apiBaseUrl = "https://${owner}-orderprocessing-api-xyapp-${envSuffix}.azurewebsites.net"
          "apiBaseUrl=$apiBaseUrl" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT
          Write-Host "Resolved API base URL: $apiBaseUrl"

      - name: Install frontend dependencies
        working-directory: frontend
        run: npm ci

      - name: Typecheck frontend workspace
        working-directory: frontend
        run: npm run typecheck

      - name: Test frontend workspace
        working-directory: frontend
        run: npm run test:web

      - name: Build frontend artifact
        working-directory: frontend
        env:
          VITE_ORDERPROCESSING_API_BASE_URL: ${{ steps.resolve-target.outputs.apiBaseUrl }}
          ORDERPROCESSING_API_BASE_URL: ${{ steps.resolve-target.outputs.apiBaseUrl }}
        run: npm run build

      - name: Upload artifact
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v6
        with:
          name: react-web
          path: frontend/apps/web/dist

  deploy:
    runs-on: windows-latest
    needs: build
    timeout-minutes: 30  # Covers approval wait + deploy + health check (~8 min worst case on F1)
    # Prod approval window: set via GitHub Settings → Environments → prod → Required reviewers timeout
    environment:
      name: ${{ github.ref_name == 'main' && 'prod' || github.ref_name == 'staging' && 'staging' || 'dev' }}
    permissions:
      id-token: write
      contents: read

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v6

      - name: Check Azure Credentials
        id: check-credentials
        shell: pwsh
        env:
          CLIENT_ID: ${{ secrets.AZUREAPPSERVICE_CLIENTID }}
          TENANT_ID: ${{ secrets.AZUREAPPSERVICE_TENANTID }}
          SUBSCRIPTION_ID: ${{ secrets.AZUREAPPSERVICE_SUBSCRIPTIONID }}
        run: |
          # Check if credentials are available via environment variables
          $ref = "${{ github.ref }}"
          if ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/main') { $targetEnv = 'prod'; $envSuffix = 'prod' }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/staging') { $targetEnv = 'staging'; $envSuffix = 'stg' }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/dev') { $targetEnv = 'dev'; $envSuffix = 'dev' }
          else { $branch = $ref.Replace('refs/heads/',''); $targetEnv = $branch; $envSuffix = $branch }

          $hasClientId = -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($env:CLIENT_ID)
          $hasTenantId = -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($env:TENANT_ID)
          $hasSubscriptionId = -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($env:SUBSCRIPTION_ID)
          
          if ($hasClientId -and $hasTenantId -and $hasSubscriptionId) {
            Write-Host "✅ Azure credentials found" -ForegroundColor Green
            "credentialsConfigured=true" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT
          } else {
            Write-Host "╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗" -ForegroundColor Yellow
            Write-Host "║         AZURE CREDENTIALS NOT CONFIGURED                      ║" -ForegroundColor Yellow
            Write-Host "╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝" -ForegroundColor Yellow
            Write-Host ""
            Write-Host "⚠️  Deployment cannot proceed - Azure credentials are missing" -ForegroundColor Yellow
            Write-Host ""
            Write-Host "Required secrets for the '$targetEnv' GitHub environment (Azure suffix '$envSuffix'):" -ForegroundColor Cyan
            Write-Host "  AZUREAPPSERVICE_CLIENTID       : $(if ($hasClientId) { '✅ Present' } else { '❌ Missing' })" -ForegroundColor $(if ($hasClientId) { "Green" } else { "Red" })
            Write-Host "  AZUREAPPSERVICE_TENANTID       : $(if ($hasTenantId) { '✅ Present' } else { '❌ Missing' })" -ForegroundColor $(if ($hasTenantId) { "Green" } else { "Red" })
            Write-Host "  AZUREAPPSERVICE_SUBSCRIPTIONID : $(if ($hasSubscriptionId) { '✅ Present' } else { '❌ Missing' })" -ForegroundColor $(if ($hasSubscriptionId) { "Green" } else { "Red" })
            Write-Host ""
            Write-Host "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" -ForegroundColor Cyan
            Write-Host "📋 TO FIX THIS:" -ForegroundColor Cyan
            Write-Host "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" -ForegroundColor Cyan
            Write-Host ""
            Write-Host "1. Run the Azure Initial Setup workflow to configure OIDC and GitHub secrets:" -ForegroundColor White
            Write-Host "   https://github.com/${{ github.repository }}/actions/workflows/azure-initial-setup.yml" -ForegroundColor Gray
            Write-Host ""
            Write-Host "2. Select 'Run workflow' and configure:" -ForegroundColor White
            Write-Host "   - Environment: all (recommended)" -ForegroundColor Gray
            Write-Host "   - Setup GitHub App: true only if APP_ID / APP_PRIVATE_KEY are missing" -ForegroundColor Gray
            Write-Host "   - Setup Azure OIDC: true" -ForegroundColor Gray
            Write-Host "   - Configure secrets: true" -ForegroundColor Gray
            Write-Host ""
            Write-Host "3. If the target app or resource group does not exist yet, run Azure Bootstrap & Deploy with Bootstrap Infrastructure checked" -ForegroundColor White
            Write-Host "   https://github.com/${{ github.repository }}/actions/workflows/azure-bootstrap.yml" -ForegroundColor Gray
            Write-Host ""
            Write-Host "4. Re-run this deployment" -ForegroundColor White
            Write-Host ""
            Write-Host "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" -ForegroundColor Gray
            Write-Host ""
            Write-Host "ℹ️  Skipping deployment (credentials not configured)" -ForegroundColor Yellow
            Write-Host ""
            "credentialsConfigured=false" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT
            exit 0
          }
      
      - name: Set target web app name
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true'
        shell: pwsh
        run: |
          $ref = "${{ github.ref }}"
          $owner = "${{ github.repository_owner }}"
          if ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/main') { $name = "$owner-orderprocessing-ui-xyapp-prod" }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/staging') { $name = "$owner-orderprocessing-ui-xyapp-stg" }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/dev') { $name = "$owner-orderprocessing-ui-xyapp-dev" }
          else { $branch = $ref.Replace('refs/heads/',''); $name = "$owner-orderprocessing-ui-xyapp-$branch" }
          echo "AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME=$name" >> $env:GITHUB_ENV
          Write-Host "Deploying to WebApp: $name"

      - name: Download artifact
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true'
        uses: actions/download-artifact@v8
        with:
          name: react-web
          path: ${{ env.FRONTEND_ARTIFACT_PATH }}

      - name: Login to Azure
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true'
        uses: azure/login@v3
        with:
          client-id: ${{ secrets.AZUREAPPSERVICE_CLIENTID }}
          tenant-id: ${{ secrets.AZUREAPPSERVICE_TENANTID }}
          subscription-id: ${{ secrets.AZUREAPPSERVICE_SUBSCRIPTIONID }}

      - name: Check Target Infrastructure Exists
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true'
        id: check-target
        shell: pwsh
        run: |
          $ref = "${{ github.ref }}"
          if ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/main') { $targetEnv = 'prod'; $envSuffix = 'prod' }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/staging') { $targetEnv = 'staging'; $envSuffix = 'stg' }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'refs/heads/dev') { $targetEnv = 'dev'; $envSuffix = 'dev' }
          else { $branch = $ref.Replace('refs/heads/',''); $targetEnv = $branch; $envSuffix = $branch }

          $rgName = "rg-orderprocessing-$envSuffix"
          $appName = "${{ env.AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME }}"

          "resourceGroupName=$rgName" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT
          "targetEnvironment=$targetEnv" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT
          "resourceSuffix=$envSuffix" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT

          Write-Host "Resolved target: GitHub environment '$targetEnv' / Azure resource suffix '$envSuffix'" -ForegroundColor Cyan

          $groupExists = az group exists --name $rgName
          if ($groupExists -ne 'true') {
            Write-Host "⚠️  Target resource group '$rgName' does not exist. Skipping deployment." -ForegroundColor Yellow
            Write-Host "ℹ️  Bootstrap the $targetEnv environment before merging branch changes that should deploy there." -ForegroundColor Yellow
            "infraReady=false" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT
            Add-Content -Path $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY -Value "## Deployment Skipped - Environment Not Bootstrapped`n- GitHub environment: $targetEnv`n- Azure resource suffix: $envSuffix`n- Resource group missing: $rgName`n- Expected app service: $appName`n- Run Azure Bootstrap & Deploy with bootstrapInfra=true for this environment, then re-run deployment.`n"
            exit 0
          }

          $webAppId = az webapp show --name $appName --resource-group $rgName --query id -o tsv 2>$null
          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0 -or [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($webAppId)) {
            Write-Host "⚠️  Target app service '$appName' does not exist in '$rgName'. Skipping deployment." -ForegroundColor Yellow
            Write-Host "ℹ️  Bootstrap may not have been run for $targetEnv, or the app was deleted separately." -ForegroundColor Yellow
            "infraReady=false" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT
            Add-Content -Path $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY -Value "## Deployment Skipped - App Service Missing`n- GitHub environment: $targetEnv`n- Azure resource suffix: $envSuffix`n- Resource group: $rgName`n- Missing app service: $appName`n- Run Azure Bootstrap & Deploy with bootstrapInfra=true for this environment, then re-run deployment.`n"
            exit 0
          }

          Write-Host "✅ Target infrastructure exists: $rgName / $appName" -ForegroundColor Green
          "infraReady=true" >> $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT

      - name: Deploy to Azure Web App
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true' && steps.check-target.outputs.infraReady == 'true'
        id: deploy-to-webapp
        uses: azure/webapps-deploy@v3
        with:
          app-name: ${{ env.AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME }}
          package: ${{ env.FRONTEND_ARTIFACT_PATH }}

      - name: Health Check
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true' && steps.check-target.outputs.infraReady == 'true'
        shell: pwsh
        run: |
          $uiUrl = "https://${{ env.AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME }}.azurewebsites.net/customers"

          Write-Host "Testing frontend route: $uiUrl" -ForegroundColor Cyan
          $healthy = $false
          $maxAttempts = 6
          for ($attempt = 1; $attempt -le $maxAttempts; $attempt++) {
            try {
              $response = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $uiUrl -Method Get -TimeoutSec 60
              if ($response.StatusCode -eq 200 -and $response.Content -match 'id="root"') {
                Write-Host "✅ Frontend responded with status: $($response.StatusCode)" -ForegroundColor Green
                Write-Host "Frontend is accessible at: $uiUrl" -ForegroundColor Cyan
                $healthy = $true
                break
              }

              Write-Host "  Attempt $attempt/$maxAttempts returned an unexpected payload." -ForegroundColor Yellow
            } catch {
              Write-Host "  Attempt $attempt/$maxAttempts failed: $($_.Exception.Message)" -ForegroundColor Yellow
              if ($attempt -lt $maxAttempts) {
                Write-Host "  Retrying in 20 s..." -ForegroundColor Yellow
                Start-Sleep -Seconds 20
              }
            }
          }
          if (-not $healthy) {
            Write-Host "❌ Frontend health check FAILED after $maxAttempts attempts" -ForegroundColor Red
          }

          if (-not $healthy) {
            Write-Host "" -ForegroundColor Gray
            Write-Host "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" -ForegroundColor Red
            Write-Host "❌ DEPLOYMENT HEALTH CHECK FAILED" -ForegroundColor Red
            Write-Host "   The React frontend did not respond after deployment. Check App Service logs." -ForegroundColor Red
            Write-Host "   URL: $uiUrl" -ForegroundColor Red
            Write-Host "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" -ForegroundColor Red
            exit 1
          }

      - name: Warm up UI before browser smoke test
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true' && steps.check-target.outputs.infraReady == 'true'
        shell: pwsh
        run: |
          $minimumUiWarmupSeconds = 300
          Write-Host "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" -ForegroundColor Cyan
          Write-Host "UI PRE-SMOKE WARM-UP BUFFER" -ForegroundColor Cyan
          Write-Host "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" -ForegroundColor Cyan
          Write-Host "Waiting $minimumUiWarmupSeconds seconds (5 minutes) before browser smoke validation starts..." -ForegroundColor Yellow
          Write-Host "Reason: freshly deployed App Service instances can serve the shell before the runtime is fully warm." -ForegroundColor Gray
          Start-Sleep -Seconds $minimumUiWarmupSeconds
          Write-Host "✅ Minimum UI warm-up buffer complete." -ForegroundColor Green

      - name: Wait for API runtime bootstrap dependency
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true' && steps.check-target.outputs.infraReady == 'true'
        shell: pwsh
        run: |
          $apiBaseUrl = "${{ needs.build.outputs.apiBaseUrl }}"
          $runtimeConfigurationUrl = "$apiBaseUrl/api/v1/Info/runtime-configuration"
          $customersUrl = "$apiBaseUrl/api/v1/Customer/GetAllCustomers"
          $headers = @{ "X-Tenant-Code" = "TenantA" }
          $overallPreSmokeBudgetSeconds = 900
          $minimumUiWarmupSeconds = 300
          $retryIntervalSeconds = 30
          $apiPollingBudgetSeconds = $overallPreSmokeBudgetSeconds - $minimumUiWarmupSeconds
          $deadline = (Get-Date).AddSeconds($apiPollingBudgetSeconds)

          Write-Host "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" -ForegroundColor Cyan
          Write-Host "WAITING FOR API DEPENDENCY BEFORE UI SMOKE TEST" -ForegroundColor Cyan
          Write-Host "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" -ForegroundColor Cyan
          Write-Host "The UI smoke test depends on the API runtime bootstrap and customer endpoints." -ForegroundColor Gray
          Write-Host "Overall pre-smoke wait policy: 5 minutes UI warm-up + up to 10 additional minutes API wait = 15 minutes hard maximum." -ForegroundColor Yellow
          Write-Host "API retry interval: $retryIntervalSeconds seconds" -ForegroundColor Yellow
          Write-Host "Runtime bootstrap URL: $runtimeConfigurationUrl" -ForegroundColor Cyan
          Write-Host "Customer directory URL: $customersUrl" -ForegroundColor Cyan

          $apiReady = $false
          $attempt = 0
          while ((Get-Date) -lt $deadline) {
            $attempt += 1
            $remainingSeconds = [Math]::Max([int][Math]::Ceiling(($deadline - (Get-Date)).TotalSeconds), 0)
            Write-Host "Attempt $attempt — checking whether the API is up for UI smoke validation (remaining budget: ${remainingSeconds}s)..." -ForegroundColor Yellow

            try {
              $runtimeConfiguration = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri $runtimeConfigurationUrl -Headers $headers -Method Get -TimeoutSec 60 -ErrorAction Stop
              $customersResponse = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $customersUrl -Headers $headers -Method Get -TimeoutSec 60 -ErrorAction Stop

              if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($runtimeConfiguration.activeTenantCode) -and $customersResponse.StatusCode -eq 200) {
                Write-Host "✅ API dependency is ready for UI smoke validation" -ForegroundColor Green
                Write-Host "   Active tenant: $($runtimeConfiguration.activeTenantCode)" -ForegroundColor Gray
                $apiReady = $true
                break
              }

              Write-Host "  Attempt $attempt returned an incomplete API payload." -ForegroundColor Yellow
            } catch {
              Write-Host "  Attempt $attempt failed: $($_.Exception.Message)" -ForegroundColor Yellow
            }

            if ((Get-Date).AddSeconds($retryIntervalSeconds) -lt $deadline) {
              Write-Host "  API is not up yet. Retrying in $retryIntervalSeconds seconds..." -ForegroundColor Yellow
              Start-Sleep -Seconds $retryIntervalSeconds
            }
          }

          if (-not $apiReady) {
            Write-Host "❌ API dependency did not become ready before the browser smoke test budget expired" -ForegroundColor Red
            Write-Host "   Wait policy exhausted: 5 minutes UI warm-up + 10 minutes API retry budget = 15 minutes total." -ForegroundColor Red
            Write-Host "   This commonly means the API deployment, migration path, or App Service warm-up is still in progress while the UI deployment has already finished." -ForegroundColor Red
            Write-Host "   Runtime URL: $runtimeConfigurationUrl" -ForegroundColor Red
            Write-Host "   Customers URL: $customersUrl" -ForegroundColor Red
            exit 1
          }

      - name: Set up Node.js for browser smoke test
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true' && steps.check-target.outputs.infraReady == 'true'
        uses: actions/setup-node@v6
        with:
          node-version: ${{ env.NODE_VERSION }}
          cache: npm
          cache-dependency-path: frontend/package-lock.json

      - name: Install frontend dependencies for browser smoke test
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true' && steps.check-target.outputs.infraReady == 'true'
        working-directory: frontend
        run: npm ci

      - name: Install Playwright Chromium
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true' && steps.check-target.outputs.infraReady == 'true'
        working-directory: frontend/apps/web
        run: npx playwright install chromium

      - name: Browser Smoke Test - Tenant Bootstrap
        if: steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured == 'true' && steps.check-target.outputs.infraReady == 'true'
        working-directory: frontend
        run: npm run smoke:web:tenant -- --url "https://${{ env.AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME }}.azurewebsites.net/customers"

      # Backend tests remain owned by deploy-api-to-azure.yml.
      # Frontend regression tests run in the build job above so tenant bootstrap issues
      # are blocked before artifact upload and deployment, and the browser smoke test
      # above validates the deployed UI respects runtime bootstrap tenants.

      - name: Deployment Summary
        if: always()
        shell: pwsh
        run: |
          $ref    = "${{ github.ref_name }}"
          $owner  = "${{ github.repository_owner }}"
          if ($ref -eq 'main') { $defaultTargetEnv = 'prod'; $defaultEnvSuffix = 'prod' }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'staging') { $defaultTargetEnv = 'staging'; $defaultEnvSuffix = 'stg' }
          elseif ($ref -eq 'dev') { $defaultTargetEnv = 'dev'; $defaultEnvSuffix = 'dev' }
          else { $defaultTargetEnv = $ref; $defaultEnvSuffix = $ref }

          $defaultApp = "$owner-orderprocessing-ui-xyapp-$defaultEnvSuffix"
          $defaultRg = "rg-orderprocessing-$defaultEnvSuffix"
          $app = if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace("${{ env.AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME }}")) { $defaultApp } else { "${{ env.AZURE_WEBAPP_NAME }}" }
          $rg = if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace("${{ steps.check-target.outputs.resourceGroupName }}")) { $defaultRg } else { "${{ steps.check-target.outputs.resourceGroupName }}" }
          $targetEnv = if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace("${{ steps.check-target.outputs.targetEnvironment }}")) { $defaultTargetEnv } else { "${{ steps.check-target.outputs.targetEnvironment }}" }
          $envSuffix = if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace("${{ steps.check-target.outputs.resourceSuffix }}")) { $defaultEnvSuffix } else { "${{ steps.check-target.outputs.resourceSuffix }}" }
          $run    = "${{ github.run_id }}"
          $repo   = "${{ github.repository }}"
          $actor  = "${{ github.actor }}"
          $event  = "${{ github.event_name }}"
          $sha    = "${{ github.sha }}".Substring(0, 7)
          $credentialsConfigured = "${{ steps.check-credentials.outputs.credentialsConfigured }}"
          $infraReady = "${{ steps.check-target.outputs.infraReady }}"
          $appUrl = if ($credentialsConfigured -ne 'true') {
            "https://$app.azurewebsites.net (target URL; deployment skipped before Azure login)"
          } elseif ($infraReady -ne 'true') {
            "https://$app.azurewebsites.net (target URL; app not provisioned yet)"
          } else {
            "https://$app.azurewebsites.net"
          }

          $status = if ($credentialsConfigured -ne 'true') {
            '⏭️ SKIPPED - credentials missing'
          } elseif ($infraReady -ne 'true') {
            '⏭️ SKIPPED - environment not bootstrapped'
          } elseif ('${{ job.status }}' -eq 'success') {
            '✅ SUCCESS'
          } else {
            '❌ FAILED'
          }

          "## 🚀 UI Deployment Summary" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| Field | Value |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "|-------|-------|" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| Status | $status |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| Branch | ``$ref`` |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| Commit | ``$sha`` |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| Triggered by | $actor ($event) |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| GitHub Environment | ``$targetEnv`` |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| Azure Resource Suffix | ``$envSuffix`` |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| Resource Group | ``$rg`` |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| App Service | ``$app`` |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| URL | $appUrl |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "| Run | [View run](https://github.com/$repo/actions/runs/$run) |" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          "> Note: This workflow does not run solution tests. API workflow owns Domain/Application/API/Architecture test execution." >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY

          if ($infraReady -ne 'true' -and $credentialsConfigured -eq 'true') {
            "" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
            "> Run Azure Bootstrap & Deploy with bootstrapInfra=true for this branch environment before expecting push-based deployments to succeed." >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          } elseif ($credentialsConfigured -ne 'true') {
            "" >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
            "> Run Azure Initial Setup with Setup Azure OIDC=true and Configure GitHub Secrets=true before rerunning this deployment." >> $env:GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
          }
</file>

<file path=".github/workflows/README-PUBLISH-TEMPLATE-PACKAGE.md">
# Publish Template Package Workflow

## Overview
Manual workflow that packs `XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates`, validates the packaged `dotnet new` flow end to end, uploads the `.nupkg` as a workflow artifact, and optionally pushes the validated package to NuGet.org or GitHub Packages.

## Why this exists
- The template must be validated from the packaged `.nupkg`, not just from the source tree.
- A publish action should not bypass the smoke path that installs the package, generates a solution, and builds the generated output.
- Operators need a safe dry-run mode that produces the final package artifact without pushing it anywhere.

## Governance handoff
This workflow is the publication endpoint, not the first signal that a new NuGet template line is needed.

Automatic detection now lives in [README-VALIDATE-TEMPLATE-PACKAGE-GOVERNANCE.md](./README-VALIDATE-TEMPLATE-PACKAGE-GOVERNANCE.md):
- Pull requests that change `templates/xy-saas/` or `templates/XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates/` must bump `PackageVersion`.
- Pushes to `dev`, `staging`, or `main` that touch the same Layer 1 template surface also run automatic packaged smoke validation.
- Those pull requests also run packaged smoke validation before merge.

That keeps template version drift from becoming a one-time manual habit.

## Trigger
Manual dispatch only.

### Run from GitHub UI
1. Open `Actions`.
2. Select `Publish Template Package`.
3. Choose the branch or tag to publish from.
4. Set `publish-package`:
   - `false` to pack, validate, and upload the `.nupkg` artifact only.
   - `true` to also push the validated package to the selected registry.
5. Select `package-source`:
   - `nuget.org`
   - `github-packages`

### Run from GitHub CLI
```bash
# Dry run: pack + smoke validate + upload artifact only
gh workflow run publish-template-package.yml \
  --ref dev \
  -f publish-package=false \
  -f package-source=nuget.org

# Publish validated package to NuGet.org
gh workflow run publish-template-package.yml \
  --ref dev \
  -f publish-package=true \
  -f package-source=nuget.org
```

## Workflow behavior

### Pack and validate
The first job always runs and performs the release-quality checks:
- `dotnet pack templates/XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates/XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates.csproj -c Release --nologo`
- `dotnet new uninstall XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates` (best effort)
- `dotnet new install <packed-nupkg>`
- `dotnet new xy-saas ...`
- `dotnet build <generated-solution> --nologo`
- Uploads the final `.nupkg` as the `template-package` artifact

### Publish
The second job runs only when `publish-package=true`.

#### NuGet.org
Requires repository secret `NUGET_API_KEY`.

```powershell
dotnet nuget push <nupkg> \
  --api-key <NUGET_API_KEY> \
  --source https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json \
  --skip-duplicate
```

#### GitHub Packages
Uses the built-in workflow `GITHUB_TOKEN` and writes to:

```text
https://nuget.pkg.github.com/<owner>/index.json
```

## Required secrets

### Always available
- `GITHUB_TOKEN` for artifact access and optional GitHub Packages publication

### Required only for NuGet.org publication
- `NUGET_API_KEY`

## Artifacts
- `template-package` — the packed `XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates.<version>.nupkg`

## When to use it
- Formal template releases such as `1.0.0`, `1.1.0`, and later immutable package lines
- Dry-run validation before publishing to a public registry
- Repeatable regeneration of the final `.nupkg` from a tagged baseline

## How consumers install from NuGet.org

Install a specific version:

```powershell
dotnet new install XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates::1.0.1
```

Check for template updates:

```powershell
dotnet new update --check-only
```

Remove the currently installed package:

```powershell
dotnet new uninstall XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates
```

## Related documentation
- [Workflow index](./README.md)
- [Validate template package governance](./README-VALIDATE-TEMPLATE-PACKAGE-GOVERNANCE.md)
- [Branch + blueprint strategy](../../docs/internal/branch-and-blueprint-strategy.md)
- [ADR-018 blueprint and snapshot strategy](../../docs/architecture/decisions/ADR-018-blueprint-and-snapshot-strategy.md)
</file>

<file path=".github/workflows/README.md">
# GitHub Actions Workflows - CI/CD Automation

This directory contains GitHub Actions workflows for automated CI/CD deployment to Azure App Services using OIDC authentication.

## 📋 Overview

This repo uses a small set of primary operational workflows, with additional support workflows for setup, validation, and troubleshooting.

| Workflow | Triggers On | Deploys To | Description |
|----------|-------------|------------|-------------|
| `ci.yml` | Pull requests to dev/staging/main | Validation only | PR build/test gate for the .NET solution plus React frontend typecheck, tests, and build |
| `azure-initial-setup.yml` | Manual | One-time setup | **[See README-AZURE-INITIAL-SETUP.md](./README-AZURE-INITIAL-SETUP.md)** - Phase 0 (GitHub App), Phase 1a (OIDC), Phase 1b (secrets) |
| `azure-bootstrap.yml` | Manual | Infrastructure + deploy | **[See README-AZURE-BOOTSTRAP.md](./README-AZURE-BOOTSTRAP.md)** - Phase 2 (infrastructure), API/UI deploy, Phase X (cleanup) |
| `configure-github-secrets.yml` | Called by initial-setup | Secret configuration | **[See README-CONFIGURE-GITHUB-SECRETS.md](./README-CONFIGURE-GITHUB-SECRETS.md)** - GitHub App setup and secret management (can run independently) |
| `infra-deploy.yml` | Manual | dev/staging/prod | **[See README-INFRA-DEPLOY.md](./README-INFRA-DEPLOY.md)** - Deploys Bicep infrastructure with manual workflow dispatch |
| `validate-deployment.yml` | Called by infra-deploy | Reusable workflow | **[See README-VALIDATE-DEPLOYMENT.md](./README-VALIDATE-DEPLOYMENT.md)** - Pre-deployment validation workflow |
| `test-validate-deployment.yml` | Manual or PR changes | Test only | **[Quick Start](./QUICK-START-TEST-VALIDATION.md)** \| **[Full Docs](./README-TEST-VALIDATE-DEPLOYMENT.md)** - Tests validation workflow independently |
| `deploy-api-to-azure.yml` | API/Backend code changes | All branches (dev/staging/main) | Builds and deploys API to environment-specific Azure Web App |
| `deploy-ui-to-azure.yml` | React frontend changes | All branches (dev/staging/main) | Builds and deploys the React frontend to the environment-specific Azure UI App Service, then runs a browser smoke check against the deployed tenant bootstrap flow |
| `publish-template-package.yml` | Manual | Artifact only or package registry | **[See README-PUBLISH-TEMPLATE-PACKAGE.md](./README-PUBLISH-TEMPLATE-PACKAGE.md)** - Packs `XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates`, validates the packaged `dotnet new` smoke flow, uploads the `.nupkg`, and optionally publishes it |
| `validate-template-package-governance.yml` | Pull requests for Layer 1 template changes, or manual | Validation only | **[See README-VALIDATE-TEMPLATE-PACKAGE-GOVERNANCE.md](./README-VALIDATE-TEMPLATE-PACKAGE-GOVERNANCE.md)** - Forces a `PackageVersion` decision for Layer 1 template changes and runs packaged smoke validation |
| `validate-adrs.yml` | ADR file, script, or lint config changes | Push/PR to main/dev/staging, or manual | **[See README-VALIDATE-ADRS.md](./README-VALIDATE-ADRS.md)** — Validates ADR filename pattern, H1 heading, `**Status:**` frontmatter, and markdownlint rules |
| `validate-ai-customization.yml` | Shared AI customization changes | Push/PR to main/dev/staging, or manual | Validates shared Copilot instructions, prompts, agents, operating-model docs, and their discovery surfaces |
| `validate-doc-links.yml` | Docs or validator changes | Push/PR to main/dev/staging, or manual | Validates local markdown links and heading anchors for the canonical `docs/` tree |

### Workflow Categories

**Primary workflows** are the workflows the team should think about first for normal delivery and operations:

| Workflow | Role |
|----------|------|
| `ci.yml` | PR gate for build and unit/architecture test validation |
| `azure-initial-setup.yml` | One-time repository and OIDC bootstrap |
| `azure-bootstrap.yml` | Main day-to-day environment bootstrap and coordinated deployment entrypoint |
| `deploy-api-to-azure.yml` | Normal API deployment path for code changes |
| `deploy-ui-to-azure.yml` | Active React frontend deployment path for the Azure UI App Service |

**Support workflows** exist for specialized validation, secondary entrypoints, or troubleshooting rather than the default delivery path:

| Workflow | Role |
|----------|------|
| `configure-github-secrets.yml` | Secondary/manual secret configuration and GitHub App troubleshooting path |
| `infra-deploy.yml` | Infra-only Bicep deployment entrypoint |
| `publish-template-package.yml` | Manual package publication path for the Layer 1 `dotnet new` template after packaged smoke validation |
| `validate-template-package-governance.yml` | Automatic PR guardrail that requires a package-version decision and packaged smoke validation for Layer 1 template changes |
| `validate-deployment.yml` | Reusable preflight validation called by infra deployment |
| `test-validate-deployment.yml` | Independent test harness for validation workflow changes |
| `validate-adrs.yml` | Documentation governance for ADR changes |
| `validate-ai-customization.yml` | Governance guardrail for shared AI operating assets |
| `validate-doc-links.yml` | Lightweight guardrail for canonical docs navigation integrity |

### Branch-to-Environment Mapping

| Git Branch | API Deployment Target | React Frontend Target |
|------------|----------------------|-----------------------|
| `dev` | orderprocessing-api-xyapp-dev | orderprocessing-ui-xyapp-dev |
| `staging` | orderprocessing-api-xyapp-stg | orderprocessing-ui-xyapp-stg |
| `main` | orderprocessing-api-xyapp-prod | orderprocessing-ui-xyapp-prod |

Workflow YAML still enforces this policy explicitly.
Azure deployment scripts consume the same defaults from `Resources/Azure-Deployment/branch-policy.json`; if governance changes, update the workflow guards and the shared policy file together.

---

## 🔐 Required GitHub Secrets

Before workflows can execute, the following secrets must be configured:

**Repository secrets**

| Secret Name | Description | How to Get |
|-------------|-------------|------------|
| `APP_ID` | GitHub App ID | GitHub App setup |
| `APP_PRIVATE_KEY` | GitHub App private key | GitHub App setup |
| `NUGET_API_KEY` | NuGet.org publish key for `XYDataLabs.SaaS.Templates` | Create in NuGet.org account settings (required only when publishing to NuGet.org) |

**Environment secrets** (`dev`, `staging`, `prod`)

| Secret Name | Description | How to Get |
|-------------|-------------|------------|
| `AZUREAPPSERVICE_CLIENTID` | Azure AD App Registration Client ID | Azure Initial Setup (Phase 1b) |
| `AZUREAPPSERVICE_TENANTID` | Azure AD Tenant ID | Azure Initial Setup (Phase 1b) |
| `AZUREAPPSERVICE_SUBSCRIPTIONID` | Azure Subscription ID | Azure Initial Setup (Phase 1b) |

### Automatic Secret Configuration

If you ran Azure Initial Setup successfully, the environment OIDC secrets are **already configured**.

Verify at: `Settings → Environments → dev/staging/prod`

### Manual Secret Configuration

If automatic configuration failed:

1. Run **Azure Initial Setup** with `configureSecrets=true`
2. **Navigate to**: Repository → Settings → Environments
3. **Open each environment** and confirm the three `AZUREAPPSERVICE_*` secrets are present

---

## 🚀 Workflow Execution

### Automatic Triggers

Workflows trigger automatically based on **what code changed**:

```bash
# Change API code and push → triggers deploy-api-to-azure.yml
git add XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.API/
git commit -m "feat: Update API endpoint"
git push origin dev  # Deploys API only to dev environment

# Change React web code and push → triggers deploy-ui-to-azure.yml
git add frontend/
git commit -m "feat: Update React payment flow"
git push origin dev  # Deploys the React frontend to the dev UI App Service

# Change API plus React frontend → triggers BOTH deploy workflows in parallel
git add XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.API/ frontend/
git commit -m "feat: Update API and React frontend"
git push origin dev  # Deploys API and the React frontend to dev environment
```

### Path-Based Triggering

**API Workflow** (`deploy-api-to-azure.yml`) triggers on changes to:
- `XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.API/**`
- `XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Application/**`
- `XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Domain/**`
- `XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.Infrastructure/**`
- `XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.SharedKernel/**`

**UI Workflow** (`deploy-ui-to-azure.yml`) triggers on changes to:
- `frontend/**`
- `Resources/Configuration/**`
- `.github/workflows/deploy-ui-to-azure.yml`

### Pull Request Behavior

**IMPORTANT**: Workflows do **NOT** trigger on Pull Request events.

- ❌ Opening a PR does **not** trigger deployment
- ❌ Merging a PR via GitHub UI does **not** trigger deployment (unless merge creates a push event)
- ✅ Merging via command line with push **does** trigger deployment:
  ```bash
  git checkout staging
  git merge dev
  git push origin staging  # ← This triggers deploy-staging.yml
  ```

### Manual Triggers

Workflows can be triggered manually via GitHub Actions UI:

1. Navigate to: **Actions** tab → Select workflow
2. Click **Run workflow** button
3. Select branch → Click **Run workflow**

---

## 📦 Workflow Stages

The API workflow and the React frontend workflow execute in 2 stages:

### Stage 1: Build (Windows Runner)
- ✅ Checkout code
- ✅ Setup Node.js 20
- ✅ Restore npm workspace dependencies
- ✅ Run frontend typecheck
- ✅ Run frontend regression tests
- ✅ Build the React production artifact with the environment-specific API base URL
- ✅ Upload build artifact

### Stage 2: Deploy (Windows Runner)
- ✅ Determine target environment (dev/staging/prod) from branch name
- ✅ Download build artifact
- ✅ Login to Azure using OIDC (passwordless authentication)
- ✅ Deploy to environment-specific Azure Web App
- ✅ Run SPA route health checks (API: `/health/ready`, frontend: `/customers`)
- ✅ Run a browser smoke check that seeds a stale tenant and verifies the deployed UI still resolves the API bootstrap tenant
- ✅ Display deployment URLs

---

## 🔍 Monitoring Deployments

