# Deferred Work Log

Use this register for justified deferrals that remain open after `/XYDataLabs-completion-check` or any other shared governance workflow.

## Rules

1. Every open item needs an owner.
2. Every open item needs a review date.
3. Every open item needs a closure trigger, not just a vague future intent.
4. Closed items stay visible until the next deliberate cleanup pass so the repo retains an audit trail.

## Open Items

| ID | Item | Source | Owner | Rationale | Risk if delayed | Review date | Closure trigger | Status |
|----|------|--------|-------|-----------|-----------------|-------------|-----------------|--------|
| DW-001 | Introduce `Address` value object where it crosses a real aggregate or request boundary | Phase 7 closeout | Phase 8 feature owner | The value object has no stable boundary anchor yet; adding it now would be speculative | Rework and churn if modeled against the wrong boundary | 2026-05-01 | A real aggregate or API request shape requires address behavior beyond primitive strings | Open |
| DW-004 | Formalize audit retention and redaction policy as an ADR | Audit trail planning | Architecture owner | The policy decision should be made with real retention, export, and compliance requirements in view | Audit implementation could drift without an explicit long-term policy | 2026-05-31 | Audit logging reaches compliance-sensitive retention/export scope | Open |
| DW-006 | Pilot shared MCP configuration under read-only controls | AI governance hardening | AI governance owner | Shared MCP adds capability and risk; governance and validation should land first | Uncontrolled external-tool growth or inconsistent local setups | 2026-05-31 | Approved server inventory, auth model, and read-only-first protocol are documented | Open |
| DW-007 | Add an opt-in git hook template for automatic local AI governance validation | AI governance hardening | AI governance owner | The repo now has CI enforcement and a VS Code task bundle; the automatic local hook remains optional until the team decides the extra friction is justified | Contributors may forget to run the local bundle task before push and rely on CI to catch drift | 2026-05-15 | Team agreement that deterministic local enforcement is worth the added commit friction, followed by a repo-owned hook template that mirrors the existing validators | Open |
| DW-009 | Tighten the completion-check secret scan so it distinguishes live secrets from known-safe placeholders and runtime-built strings | Phase 7 closeout / completion-check | Engineering quality owner | The current regex-based scan reports 23 matches that include workflow secret references, generated ARM JSON, runtime-composed connection strings, test literals, and the local HTTPS dev-certificate default password constant; manual review shows no committed live credentials, but the gate remains noisy | Real secret regressions can be harder to spot when every completion-check starts with a large false-positive set | 2026-05-15 | The scan patterns and/or exclusions are refined so the completion-check returns either 0 hits or a short list of actionable findings only | Open |
| DW-011 | Apply `AddTenantPaymentProviderCode` migration to the separate Tenant Registry DB when staging/prod use a split ops DB | Phase 8.6 code review (ADR-019) | Architecture owner | Local dev uses a single shared DB (no separate registry DB). ADR-019 documents the separate staging/prod registry DB as a future access-control concern; it has not been provisioned yet. The deployment path (`run-database-migrations.ps1`) currently only targets `OrderProcessingSystemDbContext`. When the separate registry DB is provisioned, the `PaymentProviderCode` column must be added to it before app startup. | `TenantRegistryService.FindByCode` will throw a `SqlException` on the `PaymentProviderCode` projection if the registry DB schema is behind the business DB schema. | 2026-07-31 | Separate registry DB is provisioned in staging; migration applied; `run-database-migrations.ps1` extended to also apply the registry DB schema or the column is added via a controlled ops script. | Open |
| DW-016 | Make payment amount and currency order-owned before production commerce use | Phase 8.7 Razorpay Checkout review | Payments module owner | Phase 8/8.7 correctly proves Razorpay hosted Checkout, callback signature verification, provider webhook verification, Inbox idempotency, and async payment convergence. However, `ProcessPaymentCommandHandler` still uses the legacy fixed `100.00` amount and default currency constants for payment records, while Razorpay order creation switches the provider request currency to INR. This is acceptable for the learning/payment-flow milestone but not for product-grade commerce. | Future module extraction could carry forward a payment API that is not anchored to an authoritative order/invoice total, causing amount/currency drift between Orders, Payments, provider requests, and audit records. | 2026-06-30 | Payments Phase 9 module extraction introduces an order/invoice-owned amount and currency contract; `ProcessPaymentCommand` no longer hardcodes amount/currency; persisted `PayinLog`, `CardTransaction`, `PaymentAttempt`, provider order request, callback reconciliation, and tests all use the same authoritative amount/currency source. | Open |

## Closed Items

Add closed items here instead of deleting them immediately when the closure itself is useful context for future reviewers.

| ID | Item | Closed date | Closure summary |
|----|------|-------------|-----------------|
| DW-005 | Add a repo-owned skills layer for repeated specialist workflows | 2026-04-07 | Added `.github/skills/README.md`, introduced the first repo-owned skill for Azure deployment operations, and extended AI validation/discovery surfaces to govern skills alongside prompts and agents. |
| DW-008 | Restore the strict `dotnet build --warnaserror` completion-check gate to green | 2026-04-10 | Re-ran the completion-check build gate. `dotnet build XYDataLabs.OrderProcessingSystem.sln --warnaserror /warnnotaserror:NU1701` now completes successfully; only the known `NU1701` package-compatibility warnings remain visible in output. |
| DW-010 | Implement Central Tenant Registry (separation of duties for payment provider assignment) | 2026-06-03 | Phase 8.6 completed. `Tenant.PaymentProviderCode` is now the authoritative routing field; `ITenantRegistry.FindByCode` is the resolver path; `DbInitializer` no longer contains routing logic; ADR-019 merged. Residual: separate staging/prod registry DB deployment path tracked as DW-011. |
| DW-002 | Broaden optimistic concurrency beyond `Order` | 2026-06-03 | Absorbed into Phase 8.7 scope — webhook handlers will mutate `PaymentAttempt` and potentially other aggregates; row-version protection must cover all webhook-mutated aggregates before Phase 8.7 closes. Architecture tests will enforce the property is present. |
| DW-003 | Add enhanced OpenTelemetry metrics for Phase 7 hardening areas | 2026-06-03 | Absorbed into Phase 8.7 scope — webhook endpoint is the natural instrumentation point: HMAC validation failures, inbox deduplication hits, handler latency per event type, and unresolvable-tenant rejections at the webhook boundary. |
| DW-012 | Webhook replay endpoint (admin-only) | 2026-06-05 | Re-process a specific provider event by resetting `InboxMessage.Status` to Received via `POST /api/v1/admin/webhook/replay/{providerEventId}`. No domain model changes required. Deferred: operational tooling, not core delivery path. |
| DW-013 | Refund and dispute webhook lifecycle handlers | 2026-06-05 | Refund events (`refund.created`, `refund.processed`, `refund.failed`) and dispute events (`payment.dispute.*`) require domain model additions: refund aggregate/state and a dispute state machine. Cannot implement or safely enable provider dashboard subscriptions idempotently without schema, tenant resolution tests, replay behavior, and Azure smoke validation. Deferred to Phase 9+ when the Payments module expands. |
| DW-014 | Webhook timestamp replay-attack mitigation | 2026-06-05 | Razorpay embeds a timestamp in the signature scheme. A 5-minute tolerance window should reject stale replayed requests. Code change in `WebhookSignatureValidator`. Deferred: low risk in dev; required before production hardening. |
| DW-015 | Azure Key Vault webhook secret values (deployment) | 2026-06-05 | `OPENPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` and `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` added as GitHub environment secrets following the same pattern as payment secrets. Bootstrap pre-flight validates both are present; `populate-keyvault-secrets.ps1` writes `Webhooks--OpenPay--Secret` and `Webhooks--Razorpay--Secret` to Key Vault automatically. |
